- AI/NLP Angle → Instead of just metrics, analyze content (e.g., sentiment of conversations, toxicity detection, trending topics in a community).

Cross-Platform Analytics → Track Discord + Twitch + Reddit simultaneously, showing how a community grows across platforms.

Predictive Analytics → Build models to predict churn (“who’s likely to leave the server”) or peak activity times.

Real-time Visualization → Use websockets + dashboards (e.g., D3.js, Grafana, or custom Rust backend) for live community analytics.

Privacy-First Approach → A self-hosted analytics bot where all data stays with the community, not on a third-party cloud.

Gamification Layer → Not just metrics, but leaderboards, engagement scores, badges, or “health scores” for communities.

Infra Focus → Show off skills by containerizing the bot, using event streaming (Kafka), or pushing analytics into a data warehouse (Snowflake/BigQuery).